KZ3 patch 1163: the lifter's FP helpers (ppu_fp_bin, ppu_fmadd_core) test the result for NaN first.

A NaN operand always gives a NaN result, so a numeric result returns after one compare and the operand checks run only when
the result is a NaN. Results are unchanged (PPU_FAST_FP path untouched). Changes the generated ppu_runtime header text, so a
relift picks it up. Test: tools/spu/test_vekta_helpers.sh compares the old and new helpers over NaN/inf/denormal/zero
combinations and random doubles, bit for bit, with a negative control.
